  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging will take hold today through about Tuesday or\nWednesday based on the GFS ensemble. Then an upper trough is \nexpected to move in Wednesday evening and keep temperatures cool \nfor a few days before temperatures gradually warm back up. There \nis a chance of thunderstorms expected to occur on Tuesday in \ncentral Montana and on Wednesday. There is low certainty at this \ntime, but a few severe thunderstorms will probably be part of the \nstory. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nOnly deviation was to the wind and wind gusts for this afternoon\nto bring them closer to NBM 90. \n\nThere is high confidence in a ridge coming in and lasting through\nTuesday.\n\nThere is moderate confidence in the timing of the thunderstorms\non Tuesday and Wednesday, and the cold front arrival on Wednesday.\n\nThere is low confidence on severe weather potential on Wednesday.",
